To find a definition when you don't know its name: one line per definition in main sources, members and constructor vals included, with its full name, file, lines, collapsed signature and size, `[N.N KB]`. Test sources' matches follow main sources', after an `-- also in test sources:` line, or when main sources hold no match, after a note saying so; when neither does, a renaming import (import a.X as Y, or a braced selector X as Y or X => Y) giving the name is named, with X's definition. A pattern whose owner is a method whose body holds the name says find lists no definition local to one, and names the show that prints its body; those notes count toward max_kb like the matches.

